//? Title: Power iteration: actual matrix products, normalization and residuals
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
The original two-by-two matrix has eigenvalues3 and1. Multiplication scales the
corresponding components differently; normalization keeps an iterate bounded. A
native explicit-start overload now captures each actual matrix product and its
normalization, so the plotted quotient trajectory is the library run itself. The
original seeded entry point remains separate from the teaching start(1,0). Small
controlled matrices expose spectral-gap, sign and stopping behavior without
introducing an unrelated dataset.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

$$ w_k=A v_k,\qquad v_{k+1}=w_k/\|w_k\|_2,\qquad \rho_k=v_k^T A v_k. $$

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/power_iteration_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/modular_exponentiation.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/integer_arithmetic.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <climits>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/number_theory.hpp>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/prufer.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/flow_diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/power_iteration.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    auto t = a::power_iteration_trace({{2, 1}, {1, 2}}, {1, 0}, 2);
    std::print("\n| actual attempt | before | actual matrix product | product norm | Rayleigh before | " "residual before | accepted |\n| ---: | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (auto &s : t.steps)
        std::print("| {} | `{}` | `{}` | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.iteration,
                   s.before, s.product, s.product_norm, s.rayleigh_before,
                   s.residual_before, s.accepted);

    g::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0}, std::format("Actual initial vector\n{}", t.initial));
    d.node("n1", {10, 0},
           std::format("Actual first matrix product\n{}", t.steps[0].product));
    d.node("n2", {20, 0},
           std::format("Actual first normalized iterate\n{}", t.steps[0].after));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/power_iteration_tiny.svg");
}
```
